sequenceDiagram
    title Eligibility rule lifecycle — cnext-hrms (fortest) against the HRCenter-DEV replica
    actor HR as HR Admin
    participant UI as Web App (localhost:3200)
    participant API as Next routes /api/workflow/admin/benefits/medical-reimbursement/eligibility
    participant DB as PostgreSQL HRCenter-DEV
    HR->>UI: open Benefits › Entitlement Rules
    UI->>API: GET /api/workflow/admin/benefits/medical-reimbursement/eligibility
    API->>DB: SELECT rules for the key's plans WHERE deleted_at IS NULL
    DB-->>API: the replica's seeded STANDARD rules
    API-->>UI: 200 rules list
    HR->>UI: create a new entitlement rule
    UI->>API: POST /api/workflow/admin/benefits/medical-reimbursement/eligibility
    API->>DB: INSERT INTO benefit_management.benefit_eligibility_rule
    DB-->>API: new row id
    API-->>UI: 200 rule carrying its database id
    HR->>UI: rename the rule and set it inactive
    UI->>API: PUT /api/workflow/admin/benefits/medical-reimbursement/eligibility/:id
    alt rule exists
        API->>DB: UPDATE the rule row, updated_by cnext-ui
        API-->>UI: 200 the updated rule
    else unknown id
        API-->>UI: 404 rule not found
    end
    HR->>UI: delete the rule
    UI->>API: DELETE /api/workflow/admin/benefits/medical-reimbursement/eligibility/:id
    API->>DB: DELETE FROM benefit_management.benefit_eligibility_rule
    API-->>UI: 200 ok
